  "final_message": "I put `channel` back, so the working tree now matches the original code. I did not re-run the ARCH-4 check, because I can't reach it from this repo. The unit tests pass (39), and that was before a one-character whitespace fix in `src/core/order.ts`.\n\n**Why I put it back:** the CI output shows `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). So something does read it, and removing it breaks that consumer. Restoring the field is the only fix I can make from here.\n\n**What I restored:**\n- `channel` on `Order`, `NewOrder` and `OrderPlaced`\n- the `CHANNELS` validation in `createOrder`\n- the `channel` parsing in `POST /orders`\n- the matching tests, plus the `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` examples\n\nI couldn't use `git revert`, because that command was blocked. I redid the edits by hand and compared the result with the commit before the removal. The only difference was a stray missing space in `src/core/order.ts`, which I fixed.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. The usual order is to drop it from that consumer's contract, then bump `OrderPlaced` to `schemaVersion` 4 and remove the field here.",
